! =============================================================================
! SaltFoss Training — Segment 6 (0:52-0:58): Off-gassing (2/2) -- vapor speciation
! =============================================================================
! Same composition as 05_offgas_1atm.ti, but at 1e-6 atm -- representative of
! a cover-gas / off-gas system pressure where vapor equilibrium actually
! matters. Now gas_ideal IS stable (~100 mol) and carries real speciation:
! mostly carrier FLi/F2Be vapor, but also UF4, ILi, Cs, CsF, CsI -- i.e. the
! volatile U and fission-product inventory becomes visible.
!
! CAVEAT to state out loud: this is the EQUILIBRIUM vapor composition, not a
! release RATE. Getting from here to an actual off-gas rate needs transport
! -- the MOOSE coupling in next session's hour.
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/saltfoss/05_offgas_lowP.ti
! Verified output (mole fraction in gas_ideal, ~99.7 mol total):
!   FLi    0.647        F2Be   0.330        UF4    9.7e-03
!   ILi    2.0e-04       Cs    1.4e-04      CsF    6.1e-05       CsI  1.2e-06
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 1200
pressure          = 1.0E-6
mass(3)           = 66.0       ! Li
mass(4)           = 33.0       ! Be
mass(92)          = 1.0        ! U
mass(55)          = 0.02       ! Cs -- volatile fission product
mass(53)          = 0.02       ! I  -- volatile fission product
mass(9)           = 135.0      ! F
temperature unit  = K
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MSD-TC_V4.1_Fluorides_No_Func.dat
print mode        = 2
